    "perMemberEvidence": "For shared English key, identityMembers is derived from each actual member’s same blocking key and an unchanged recognized identity-name kind. Chinese-only claims cannot mark that member English-supported. Unsupported English or missing specific Chinese identity evidence yields unknown member, retained in every partition.",
    "partitionSemantics": "Each known member participates in all of its own Chinese possible-equivalence partitions; unknown members join each partition. This retains known/unknown and unknown/unknown comparisons while a third weak or multi-alias bridge cannot create a known-known edge absent shared specific Chinese evidence. Empty/one-partition cases retain all members.",
    "variantSafety": "Variant equivalence is used solely to avoid pruning English candidates with potentially equivalent Chinese spellings. Exact/direct Chinese key buckets, displayed/source/name keys and alias claims remain unchanged; Chinese-only spelling variants do not become new blocking aliases.",
    "resolverSafety": "normalizeName/localNameKeys/explicitIdentityConstraints/connectedBlockComponents/resolvePeopleClusters and all identity-kind/nonblocking/weak tables remain byte-identical to canonical base. Variant classes never automatically merge people or modify constraints.",
    "conservativeDataMeaning": "Five documented Unihan relations including context-limited semantics are treated as possible equivalence under undirected/transitive closure. This can intentionally add false-positive comparisons (including ambiguous classes such as陸/六); it is not a claim of personal-name identity or exhaustive historical orthographic coverage.",
